# .dockerignore — files Docker should NOT send to the build.
#
# Why it matters: `docker build .` first uploads the whole folder (the "build
# context") to the Docker engine. Ignoring junk here:
#   - makes builds faster (less to upload),
#   - keeps images small and free of secrets (.env) or local build output,
#   - avoids breaking layer caching because some irrelevant file changed.

# Maven build output — the image builds its own jar, so never send ours
target/

# Version control and IDE files
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea
.vscode
*.iml
.DS_Store

# The Maven wrapper isn't needed: the build stage uses an image with Maven installed
.mvn
mvnw
mvnw.cmd

# Secrets and docs
.env
*.md

# The Dockerfile itself doesn't need to be inside the context
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
